{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.ChiralFermionBraidWords","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ChiralFermionBraidWords","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.leptonNumber_not_markov_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.leptonNumber_not_markov_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L193-L213","doc":"**The candidate fails the corpus's own conservation axiom.**\n\nMarkov II (stabilization) sends `β ∈ B_n` to `βσ_n ∈ B_{n+1}` with the *same*\nlink closure, and raises the writhe by `1`.  The Borromean baryon has writhe `0`\n(`writhe_borromean`), so its stabilisation has writhe `1` — and therefore\n`L = sign(writhe)` jumps from `0` to `1`.\n\n`lepton-number-categorical-properties.md` conservation clause 3 requires\n`ΔL = 0` under Markov moves.  This is `ΔL = 1`.  So `L = sign(writhe)` is **not\na function of the link**, only of the braid word, and it is refuted as a state\nfunction on Markov classes.\n\nThe one surviving reading is that states are **Gröbner–Shirshov normal forms**\n(`mba-step02-gs-reduction.md`: \"every downstream algorithm consumes `NF(w)`, not\nthe raw braid\"), where a canonical representative is fixed and Markov moves do\nnot act within the state space.  On that reading `L = sign(writhe)` is\nwell-defined — but then conservation clause 3 is about a different object than\nthis `L`, and the corpus should say which. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.Y_eq_B_sub_L_left_handed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.Y_eq_B_sub_L_left_handed","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L174-L188","doc":"**The left-handed spectrum — conditional on the quark writhe.**\n\nThe corpus supplies no quark braid word, so its writhe is carried as an explicit\nhypothesis (`hq`).  Given it, `Y = B - L` returns `{+1/3, +1/3, -1, -1}` for\n`(u, d, νₑ, e⁻)`.  Stated in the `3×` normalisation to stay division-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.Y_not_factoring_through_writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.Y_not_factoring_through_writhe","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L154-L172","doc":"**The writhe-degenerate pair, with derived writhes.**\n\nThe Borromean baryon and the gluon unit both have writhe `0` — *computed* from\ntheir braid words — while carrying different baryon number (`1` vs `0`).  Since\n`L` vanishes on both, `Y = B - L` differs on them at equal writhe, so `Y` is not\na function of the writhe.\n\nThis discharges from derived facts the hypothesis assumed by\n`sm-hypercharge-invariant.lean`'s `exists_writhe_degenerate_pair`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.leptonNumber_matches_corpus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.leptonNumber_matches_corpus","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L141-L150","doc":"**All six stated rows.**  `νₑ = σ₁`, `e⁻ = σ₁³`, their mirrors, and the two\nwrithe-`0` hadron words. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.mirror_moves_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.mirror_moves_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L125-L137","doc":"**The chirality obstruction is discharged at braid level.**\n\nFor `n ≠ 0` the particle `σ₁ⁿ` and its mirror `σ₁⁻ⁿ` have different writhes, so\nthe mirror does **not** fix the carrier.  This is exactly the hypothesis\n`LeptonNumberCarrierChirality.mirror_must_move_the_carrier` requires — and it\nholds even though `νₑ = σ₁` and `ν̄ₑ = σ₁⁻¹` both close to the (amphichiral)\nunknot.  The braid word, not the knot type, is the carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.writhe_mirror_sigma1Pow_carriers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.writhe_mirror_sigma1Pow_carriers","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L119-L123","doc":"`writhe (mirror (σ₁ⁿ)) = -n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.writhe_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.writhe_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L114-L115","doc":"Hence the Borromean baryon has writhe `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.writhe_gluon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.writhe_gluon","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L111-L112","doc":"The gluon unit is writhe-balanced: one positive and one negative crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.writhe_sigma1Pow_carriers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.writhe_sigma1Pow_carriers","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L105-L109","doc":"`writhe (σ₁ⁿ) = n` — the carrier writhes are computed, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.leptonNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.leptonNumber","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L100-L101","doc":"**Lepton number candidate**: the sign of the writhe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.borromean","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L97-L98","doc":"The Borromean baryon `B₃ = (σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.gluonUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.gluonUnit","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L94-L95","doc":"The gluon unit `σ₀σ₁⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.mirror","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L91-L92","doc":"The braid mirror `σᵢ ↦ σᵢ⁻¹`, negating every generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.sigma1Pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.sigma1Pow","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L88-L89","doc":"`σ₁ⁿ` for `n ≥ 0`, whose closure is the torus knot `T(2, n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.writhe","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L85-L86","doc":"The writhe of a braid word: the sum of the crossing signs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.BraidWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords.BraidWord","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean#L82-L83","doc":"A braid word: entry `±i` denotes the generator `σᵢ^{±1}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}